# practice-01/.dockerignore — what the Docker build context does NOT send to the daemon.
#
# The context is practice-01/ (docker/Dockerfile is built with `-f docker/Dockerfile .`
# from here), because the Dockerfile copies parser-ts/. Everything else in this folder
# would otherwise be shipped too — the Java tracks, your .env, a previous run's out/.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the LAST match wins, so a `!` line can re-include
# one file that an earlier pattern excluded. `*` does not cross `/`; `**` does.

# Dependencies and build output — the image installs its own with `npm ci`.
**/node_modules
**/.gradle
**/build

# Secrets. `.env.*` also catches .env.example; neither belongs in an image layer.
.env
.env.*

# The other acts. The bot's target is parser-ts and only parser-ts.
java
ts
parser-java

# A previous run's copy of the container (verify.sh reads it; the next build must not).
docker/out
docker/out-break-it

# Prose is not part of the target... except the one file the bot MUST see.
# `**/*.md` drops every markdown file at any depth; the negation that follows re-includes
# exactly one path. Negation works here because the parent directory (parser-ts/) is itself
# still included — Docker cannot re-include a file whose directory was excluded.
**/*.md
!parser-ts/CLAUDE.md
